# Dynamic Sales Dashboard Using Parameters

## Project Overview
This project analyzes the **Superstore Sales Dataset** (from Kaggle) to build an interactive sales dashboard and a predictive model for sales forecasting. The dashboard allows dynamic switching between key metrics (Sales, Profit, Quantity) using parameters. A Linear Regression model predicts Sales based on Discount, Quantity, and Profit.

## Dataset
- Source: [Superstore Sales Dataset on Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/vivek468/superstore-dataset-final)
- Rows: 9,994 (after cleaning ~9,525)
- Columns: 21 (Order ID, Sales, Profit, Quantity, Discount, Category, Region, etc.)

## Repository Contents
- `data_cleaning.py` – script to clean raw data (handles missing, duplicates, outliers)
- `model_training.py` – trains Linear Regression model, saves as `sales_model.pkl`
- `visualizations.py` – generates 5 charts (bar, line, pie, heatmap, scatter)
- `DSBDA_Dashboard.ipynb` – Jupyter notebook with full pipeline and explanations
- `superstore.csv` – original raw data (not included due to size, download from Kaggle)
- `clean_superstore.csv` – cleaned dataset (generated by script)
- `requirements.txt` – Python dependencies
- `README.md` – this file

